[OPT_VERBOSITY]
\par -v,\--verbosity=[0-8]
Activate loglevel. Legal values are between 0 and 8. Default loglevel
(without any \b -v option) is \b 2 which prints warnings and errors. The
following loglevels are available:
\htmlonly
<table class="m-table">
	<tr> <th>Loglevel</th> <th>Description</th>            </tr>
	<tr> <td>0</td>        <td>Quiet. No logs. Never.</td> </tr>
	<tr> <td>1</td>        <td>Errors only</td>            </tr>
	<tr> <td>2</td>        <td>Warnings</td>               </tr>
	<tr> <td>3</td>        <td>Information</td>            </tr>
	<tr> <td>4</td>        <td>Debug</td>                  </tr>
	<tr> <td>5</td>        <td>More debug</td>             </tr>
	<tr> <td>6</td>        <td>Even more debug</td>        </tr>
	<tr> <td>7</td>        <td>Too much debug</td>         </tr>
	<tr> <td>8</td>        <td>Trace</td>                  </tr>
</table>
\endhtmlonly
\manonly
.sp
.TS
tab(|);
cl.
Loglevel | Description
-------- | -----------
   0     | Quiet. No logs. Never.
   1     | Errors only
   2     | Warnings
   3     | Information
   4     | Debug
   5     | More debug
   6     | Even more debug
   7     | Too much debug
   8     | Trace
.TE
.sp
\endmanonly
For any \b n > 8, loglevel 8 will be set. Log messages will be printed to stdlog
by default. Alternatively, a logfile can be specified by option \b --l. If \b -q
is present, any other loglevel options will be ignored.
[OPT_VERBOSITY]

